ry  but if they decide to do that then the  battle might not happen till episode 4.  once the fighting does begin it's not  going to stop for a very long time  so i'm going to do a quick calculation  to work out how long it might last  if we use the overall arc as a  comparison that was 40 chapters adapted  over 16 total episodes  with many of the chapters being  action-packed just like the paranormal  liberation war  if season 6 was to average that same  pace then the battle between heroes and  villains would last up until episode 18  or 20 depending on if there's filler or  not  after those 18 to 20 episodes we'll  likely have an episode on the backstory  of hawks and the state of hero society  before going into another episode on the  backstory of derby and ending with a  cliffhanger about one for all  next we will learn about the true nature  of this power and midori would make a  huge decision about his future that will  lead us into the next arc  from there there should be about two or  three episodes remaining and this will  obviously begin the next storyline which  is focused on deku's movements after the  war  season 4 left us with the pro-hero arc  being incomplete and dabby didn't show  up until the beginning of the following  season  so in a similar fashion i think season 6  will end with deku coming face to face  with a certain villain but he won't  actually fight them until season 7.  finally when it comes to the release  date based on previous patterns season 6  will begin on the 2nd of april 2022  i say this because with the one  exception of season four every season of  my hero has released either a filler  episode or the first real episode  on the first weekend of april seasons  one two three and five all follow this  pattern  and unless production of season six is  affected by a potential fourth movie  i see no reason why it shouldn't be the  same on the off chance they are actually  making another movie though  then in theory the release date mig